        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 50,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Consider the polynomial \\(P(x) = ax^2 + bx + c\\). We know that \\(|P(x)| \\leq 1\\) for all \\(x\\) in the interval \\([0, 1]\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 370,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 372,
        "char_start": 132,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 161,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 162,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Evaluate \\(P(x)\\) at the endpoints and midpoint of the interval \\([0, 1]\\):\n- At \\(x = 0\\), \\(P(0) = c\\).\n- At \\(x = 1\\), \\(P(1) = a + b + c\\).\n- At \\(x = \\frac{1}{2}\\), \\(P\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{a}{4} + \\frac{b}{2} + c\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 542,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 544,
        "char_start": 374,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 253,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 254,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Since \\(|P(x)| \\leq 1\\) for all \\(x\\) in \\([0, 1]\\), we have:\n- \\(|c| \\leq 1\\),\n- \\(|a + b + c| \\leq 1\\),\n- \\(\\left|\\frac{a}{4} + \\frac{b}{2} + c\\right| \\leq 1\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 736,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 737,
        "char_start": 546,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 303,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 304,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: To maximize \\(|a| + |b| + |c|\\), consider the case where \\(a, b, c\\) take values that satisfy the above inequalities and try to find the maximum possible sum of their absolute values."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1101,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1103,
        "char_start": 739,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 489,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 490,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Assume \\(c = 1\\). Then \\(|a + b + 1| \\leq 1\\) and \\(\\left|\\frac{a}{4} + \\frac{b}{2} + 1\\right| \\leq 1\\). Simplify these inequalities:\n- From \\(|a + b + 1| \\leq 1\\), we get \\(-2 \\leq a + b \\leq 0\\).\n- From \\(\\left|\\frac{a}{4} + \\frac{b}{2} + 1\\right| \\leq 1\\), we get \\(-2 \\leq \\frac{a}{4} + \\frac{b}{2} \\leq 0\\), or equivalently, \\(-8 \\leq a + 2b \\leq 0\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1204,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1205,
        "char_start": 1105,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 535,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 536,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Solve the system of inequalities:\n- \\( -2 \\leq a + b \\leq 0 \\)\n- \\( -8 \\leq a + 2b \\leq 0 \\)"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1283,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1285,
        "char_start": 1207,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 562,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 563,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Subtract the first inequality from the second:\n- \\(-6 \\leq b \\leq 2\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1378,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1380,
        "char_start": 1287,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 606,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 607,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Substitute \\(b = -2\\) into \\(a + b \\leq 0\\):\n- \\(a - 2 \\leq 0 \\Rightarrow a \\leq 2\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1475,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1477,
        "char_start": 1382,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 650,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 651,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Substitute \\(b = -2\\) into \\(a + b \\geq -2\\):\n- \\(a - 2 \\geq -2 \\Rightarrow a \\geq 0\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1816,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1818,
        "char_start": 1479,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 802,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 803,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Therefore, \\(a = 2\\) and \\(b = -2\\) satisfy both inequalities. Check if this satisfies the original conditions:\n- \\(P(0) = 1\\),\n- \\(P(1) = 2 - 2 + 1 = 1\\),\n- \\(P\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{2}{4} - \\frac{2}{2} + 1 = \\frac{1}{2} - 1 + 1 = \\frac{1}{2}\\).\n\nAll conditions are satisfied. Thus, \\(|a| + |b| + |c| = 2 + 2 + 1 = 5\\)."
      }
    ]
